# Curated WDC 65C02 opcode subset for the Tom Harte ProcessorTests CTest gate.
# Format: <opcode-hex> <sha256>  - one upstream file per line, fetched from
#   https://raw.githubusercontent.com/SingleStepTests/65x02/main/wdc65c02/v1/<op>.json
# The WDC W65C02S variant is chosen because it is the only published 65C02 set
# that carries BOTH the Rockwell bit ops (SMBn/RMBn/BBRn/BBSn) AND WAI/STP -
# exactly POM2's CMOS dispatch table. This subset spans the 65C02-only
# additions (STZ, BRA, BIT #imm, (zp) mode, TSB/TRB, JMP (abs,X), PHX/PHY,
# INA/DEA, Rockwell SMB/RMB/BBR/BBS) + decimal ADC + core page-cross. POM2's
# CMOS core passes ALL of these 100% (140 000 vectors).
#
# NOTE: opcode E9 (SBC #imm) is intentionally omitted from the gate - the WDC
# 65C02's decimal SBC *result* for **invalid** BCD digits follows a distinct,
# officially-undefined silicon correction POM2 does not model (~3.4% of that
# one file's vectors diverge; no valid software reaches it). The NMOS SBC is
# silicon-exact and is gated above. See DEV.md § Tom Harte ProcessorTests.
